WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.976 --> 00:00:18.440
Will to get Paul Revere, and Vinnie and Mandy stayed to help his mother pick apples.

2
00:00:19.841 --> 00:00:22.962
Several large apple trees grew in the backyard.

3
00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:29.703
Will's mother gave them each a basket, and they all filled them with apples.

4
00:00:31.084 --> 00:00:34.065
As they worked, the children asked about England.

5
00:00:34.085 --> 00:00:40.187
"A while ago, the British passed the Stamp Act," Will's mother said.

6
00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:44.169
"We heard something about that," said Vinnie.

7
00:00:44.189 --> 00:00:52.793
"Everything we read—newspapers, magazines, books, even playing cards—must have a stamp.

8
00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.354
The stamp shows that a tax has been paid for it.

9
00:00:57.415 --> 00:01:02.428
Americans shouldn't have to pay taxes to the British," she said with feeling.

10
00:01:02.448 --> 00:01:06.029
"That's not fair," said Mandy.

11
00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:11.091
"Many people are upset," Will's mother continued.

12
00:01:11.111 --> 00:01:13.911
"And many of us spoke up.

13
00:01:14.972 --> 00:01:18.233
Some Boston men formed a group called the Sons of Liberty."

14
00:01:18.253 --> 00:01:20.313
"Are Mr.

15
00:01:20.473 --> 00:01:21.333
Adams and Mr.

16
00:01:21.393 --> 00:01:22.554
Hancock members?"

17
00:01:23.194 --> 00:01:23.834
asked Vinnie.

18
00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:26.875
Will's mother did not answer.

19
00:01:28.135 --> 00:01:30.396
She said, "It is a secret group.

20
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.702
No one knows for sure who is a member.

21
00:01:34.862 --> 00:01:37.664
But we know they are fighting for America's freedom."

22
00:01:37.684 --> 00:01:40.166
"Is that why Mr.

23
00:01:40.226 --> 00:01:41.767
Hancock was arrested?"

24
00:01:42.527 --> 00:01:43.208
asked Mandy.

25
00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:49.212
"I want to show you something," Will's mother said in a direct way.

26
00:01:50.613 --> 00:01:54.575
She carried her basket into the house and down to the basement.

27
00:01:55.996 --> 00:01:57.277
The children followed.

28
00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.240
The basement was filled with barrels of apples.

29
00:02:02.684 --> 00:02:06.525
"Wow! What are you going to do with all these apples?"

30
00:02:07.205 --> 00:02:07.825
asked Vinnie.

31
00:02:07.845 --> 00:02:11.727
"We make apple cider," she explained.

32
00:02:11.747 --> 00:02:16.048
"Our Boston apple cider is very popular in Europe.

33
00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:18.788
We ship it everywhere."

34
00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:23.730
She proudly showed them a stack of clothes, neatly folded.

35
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.270
"See these clothes?"

36
00:02:26.871 --> 00:02:27.891
said Will's mother.

37
00:02:27.911 --> 00:02:31.552
"Some women and I belong to our own group.

38
00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:34.665
We are called the Daughters of Liberty.

39
00:02:35.445 --> 00:02:37.306
We make all of our own clothes.

40
00:02:38.326 --> 00:02:40.367
We don't buy any dresses from Britain.

41
00:02:41.888 --> 00:02:45.810
Boston families don't want or need anything from Britain."

42
00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.951
Just then, Will returned.

43
00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:52.632
"We need to go now," he said simply.

44
00:02:54.253 --> 00:02:57.794
Vinnie and Mandy said good-bye to Will's mother and his sisters.

45
00:02:58.955 --> 00:03:01.196
They followed Will to the center of town.

46
00:03:02.652 --> 00:03:05.994
Beautiful brick homes with stone steps lined the streets.

47
00:03:07.275 --> 00:03:09.336
Some houses also had offices.

48
00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:16.160
They walked up to one office with a sign that read, "John Adams, Attorney."

49
00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.302
A servant opened the door.

50
00:03:19.322 --> 00:03:22.284
"Will Coats to see Mr.

51
00:03:22.444 --> 00:03:24.645
Adams," Will told the servant.

52
00:03:25.926 --> 00:03:28.968
They followed the servant into an office.

53
00:03:30.192 --> 00:03:33.855
It was beautifully decorated with polished wooden furniture.

54
00:03:35.176 --> 00:03:36.738
Portraits hung on the walls.

55
00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.799
"Is Mr.

56
00:03:38.899 --> 00:03:40.521
Adams a famous attorney?"

57
00:03:41.081 --> 00:03:41.782
asked Mandy.

58
00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:47.266
Will nodded and added, "He is also a fighter for freedom."

59
00:03:47.286 --> 00:03:54.672
"And the second president of the United States," whispered Vinnie to his sister.

60
00:03:55.993 --> 00:03:56.894
Mandy giggled.

61
00:04:00.552 --> 00:04:04.274
The servant led them to two men talking before a fireplace.

62
00:04:05.694 --> 00:04:07.735
They turned when the children walked in.

63
00:04:07.755 --> 00:04:09.456
"Come in!"

64
00:04:09.976 --> 00:04:12.958
A man with a sharp, thin nose walked toward them.

65
00:04:12.978 --> 00:04:18.300
"I'm John Adams," he said, "and this is Paul Revere."
